As suggested [here](https://github.com/tektoncd/pipeline/issues/2591#issuecomment-647754800), we can add a field - `MaxParallelTasks` - to `PipelineRunSpec` which is an integer that represents the maximum number of `Tasks` that can run concurrently in the `Pipeline`. 

type PipelineRunSpec struct {
	PipelineSpec *PipelineSpec `json:"pipelineSpec,omitempty"`
	...
	// MaxParallelTasks holds the maximum count of parallel taskruns
	// +optional
	MaxParallelTasks int `json:"maxParallelTasks,omitempty"`
}

Before scheduling a new `TaskRun` as part of the `PipelineRun`, the `PipelineRun` controller would check how many `TaskRuns` are running in the `PipelineRun`. If the count of running `TaskRuns` is less than `MaxParallelTasks`, the new `TaskRun` would be scheduled. If the count of running `TaskRuns` equals `MaxParallelTasks`, the new `TaskRun` won't be scheduled until later when another `TaskRun` is completed and the `PipelineRun` does the reconciliation again. 

```

